// Decoding a JWT conceptually:
// A JWT looks like this: eyJhbGci.eyJ1c2VySWQi.xYzSignature

// Part 1: Header (Algorithm used)
// { "alg": "HS256", "typ": "JWT" }

// Part 2: Payload (The actual data. NOT ENCRYPTED! Easily readable!)
// { "userId": 123, "role": "admin", "exp": 1678901234 }

// Part 3: Signature (The security seal)
// Created by hashing (Header + Payload + SERVER_SECRET_KEY)
// If a hacker changes 'role' to 'admin', the signature becomes completely invalid!
